# Frontend quality

Design work must ship as production-ready frontend, not as a visual mock that breaks in the browser.

## HTML and accessibility

- Semantic HTML (`header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `article`, `button`, `label`, etc.)
- Accessible interaction states (hover, focus, active, disabled, loading, error)
- Full keyboard navigation for interactive UI
- Visible focus states that match the brand without hiding them
- WCAG-conscious contrast for text, icons, and controls
- `prefers-reduced-motion` support for all non-essential animation
- No hover-only interactions required to complete tasks
- No decorative elements blocking content or intercepting clicks
- Touch targets adequate on mobile (minimum 44px where practical)

## Layout and performance

- Responsive typography (fluid scales, not fixed px-only headlines)
- Fluid layouts that do not break at intermediate widths
- Stable loading states; no layout shift from missing image dimensions
- Optimized image delivery (appropriate format, sizing, lazy load where sensible)
- Sensible animation performance (prefer transform/opacity; avoid layout-thrashing)
- No unnecessary client-side JavaScript for static presentation
- No broken mobile overflow or horizontal scroll from design choices

## Integrity

- No placeholder links (`href="#"`) on customer-facing surfaces
- No fake functionality or dead buttons
- No unresolved console errors
- No hydration errors
- No TypeScript errors introduced by design work
- No lint errors introduced by design work

## Component discipline

- No duplicated component patterns where a reusable primitive is appropriate
- No premature abstraction that erases visual distinctiveness
- The design system encodes art direction; it does not neutralize it (see `design-system-engineer` skill)

## Visual testing breakpoints

Capture and **inspect** screenshots at minimum:

| Width | Context |
| --- | --- |
| 1440px | Wide desktop |
| 1280px | Laptop |
| 1024px | Tablet landscape |
| 768px | Tablet portrait |
| 430px | Large mobile |
| 390px | Standard mobile |
| 360px | Small mobile |

Do not assume correct CSS equals correct design. Look at the screenshots.

Use `visual-qa-critic`, `responsive-art-director`, and `layout-perfection-critic` skills for structured review.

## Production hardening checklist

Before declaring design work done:

- [ ] Accessibility: focus, contrast, screen reader names, reduced motion
- [ ] Browser behavior: Chrome, Safari, Firefox spot check
- [ ] Performance: no jank from motion or images
- [ ] Type safety and lint clean
- [ ] Responsive behavior at all required breakpoints
- [ ] Loading, empty, error states implemented
- [ ] SEO and AI visibility per `seo-ai-visibility.mdc` (metadata, schema, sitemap, llms.txt)
- [ ] Pixel-perfect pass per `pixel-perfect-quality.mdc` (markdown, spacing, CWV)
- [ ] Real interactions only; no placeholder content
- [ ] No dead controls

